Name:           count()
Description:    Calculate count of a specified element in a supplied array
Input:          Array of data to serach (data), element to be counted (target)
Output:         Number of occurrences of target in data array
Complexity:     O(n) - linear

// SET UP:
Set count to 0

// LOGIC:
for each slot (i) in data:
    if data[i] == target:
        increase count by 1

// OUTPUT:
return count

Name:           maxFrequency()
Description:    Find element with highest frequency in supplied array (data)
Input:          Array of data to find most frequent value
Output:         Most frequent value
Complexity:     O(n^2) - quadratic

// SET UP:
Set maxCount to 1
Set mostFreq to first element in data (data[0])

// LOGIC:
for each element (target) in data:
    Set count to 0

    // LOGIC:
    for each slot (j) in data:
        if data[j] == target:
            increase count by 1

    if count > maxCount:
        set maxCount to count
        set mostFreq to target

OUTPUT:
return mostFreq


Name:           optimisedMaxFrequency()
Description:    Find element with highest frequency in supplied array (data)
Input:          Array of data to find most frequent value
Output:         Most frequent value
Complexity:

SETUP:
Set mostFreq to data[0]
Set maxCount to 0

Set count to 0
Set runStart to 0
Set runEnd to 0

// LOGIC:
for each slot (i) in data, ending at data length - 1:
    Increase runEnd by 1
    If data[runStart] is not equal to data[runEnd]:
        count = runEnd - runStart

        if count > maxCount:
            Set maxCount = count
            Set mostFreq = data[runStart]

        Set runStart = runEnd

// OUTPUT:
Return mostFreq